  "question": {
    "text": "A massless platform is kept on a light elastic spring, as shown in the figure. When particle of mass 0.1 kg is dropped on the pan from a height of 0.24 m, the particle sticks to the pan, and the spring is compressed by 0.01 m. From what height should the particle be dropped to cause a compression of 0.04 m?<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0077_36c9d0c03182.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 115px; height: 159px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "0.96 m",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "2.96 m",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "3.96 m",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "0.48 m",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let the particle be dropped from a height h and the spring be compressed by y. According to conservation of mechanical energy,<br br=\"\" />Loss in potential energy of the particle = gain in elastic potential energy of the spring<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&there4;</mo> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mtext>mg</mtext> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mi></mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo> <mo>+</mo> <mi>y</mi> </mrow> </mfenced> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mi>k</mi> <msup> <mi>y</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> </math><br /><br />Now, as the particle and spring remain same, hence<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mi></mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo> </mrow> <mn>1</mn> </msub> <mo>+</mo> <msub> <mi>y</mi> <mn>1</mn> </msub> </mrow> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mi></mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo> </mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>+</mo> <msub> <mi>y</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <msup> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <msub> <mi>y</mi> <mn>1</mn> </msub> </mrow> <mrow> <msub> <mi>y</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>0</mn> <mo>&middot;</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mn>4</mn> <mo>+</mo> <mn>0</mn> <mo>&middot;</mo> <mn>0</mn> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mi></mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo> </mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>+</mo> <mn>0</mn> <mo>&middot;</mo> <mn>0</mn> <mn>4</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </mfenced> <mo>=</mo> <msup> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>0</mn> <mo>&middot;</mo> <mn>0</mn> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>0</mn> <mo>&middot;</mo> <mn>0</mn> <mn>4</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> </math><br /><br />Solving we get, h<sub>2</sub> = 3.96 m"
  }
